  "activity_sections": [
    {
      "key": "8ad8bfcd-6b48-4e35-b963-2a29f373c802",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-list-alt\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Display**: Show “Reflect” slide\n\n**Reflect:** _Why is it important to give a robot specific instructions when you “program” it?_\n",
        "name": "Reflect"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "8ad8bfcd-6b48-4e35-b963-2a29f373c802",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8721519c-a5ce-4f67-9bca-8d26ec3806dc"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "1eb89911-13bd-4756-b25b-cc0fe22727f7",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "\n<i class=\"fa fa-list-alt\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Display**: Show “Vocabulary” slide\n\n- **Algorithm** - A list of steps to finish a task.\n- **Bug** - Part of a program that does not work correctly.\n- **Debugging** - Finding and fixing problems in an algorithm or program.\n- **Sequencing** - Putting commands in correct order so computers can read the commands.\n",
        "name": "Vocabulary"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "1eb89911-13bd-4756-b25b-cc0fe22727f7",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8721519c-a5ce-4f67-9bca-8d26ec3806dc"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "2e611b26-e27e-439d-87d2-377153b28fd4",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-list-alt\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Display**: Show “Bridging Activity” slide\n\nThis short activity will help students relate the ideas of persistence and debugging to the puzzles that they are about to complete online.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-list-alt\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Display**: Show “Maze Bridging” slide\n\n**Display:** Project a copy of the ***Maze Bridging Page** for the class to see.  Make sure that you have pre-placed the movement blocks in the workspace using ***Maze Blocks** in a configuration like the one below (this is already configured for you on the slide):\n\n![](https://images.code.org/ac052e9d25e77dd800fbf18871bc5fcf-image-1611178828427.47.39.png)\n\n**Model:**  Tell students that you have this workspace on display that looks just like the area that they will see when they start to do the Code.org puzzles online.  As the teacher, let them know that you are SO SMART that you already put all of the code in that you are going to need to solve this puzzle, then ask them to watch you \"Run\" it by moving your finger (or a penny, or some other indicator) along the path.\n\nIt won't be long before you run into a block of TNT.  Feign frustration.\n\n**Discuss:**\n\n- _What am I feeling right now, do you think?_\n- _Should I quit?_\n- _Should I throw all of the code away and start over?_\n\n**Think:** _How can I fix this program so that I don't run into the TNT?_\n\nUse the blocks provided on the slide and drag them into the work area to demonstrate student solutions.\n\n**Pair:** Have students work on solutions to get the bird around the TNT. Depending on your classroom, you might want to either have them fix each mistake one at a time (with demos in between) or students might feel comfortable working together to fix the entire program.\n\n**Share:** Have volunteers come up to help move the blocks into the right location.  \"Run\" the program over and over as a class, fixing bugs, until the bird does what it is supposed to.  Continue to point out experiences that relate to persistence, frustration, and debugging.\n\nWhen your class reaches the pig, celebrate not only their achievements, but their persistence!",
        "name": "Persistence and Debugging"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "2e611b26-e27e-439d-87d2-377153b28fd4",
        "lesson_activity.key": "8721519c-a5ce-4f67-9bca-8d26ec3806dc"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "f80e7e45-5a3f-4c56-a7bc-097474552538",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "description": "Students should now be ready to see a real puzzle in action!"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "f80e7e45-5a3f-4c56-a7bc-097474552538",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7684f284-70a6-4c67-8ca0-9220f05970f7"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "9348cae3-4fe2-46af-bf64-d7f8afcf9a26",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Some students may struggle with turning their bird in the correct direction, particularly when the bird isn't facing up. Remind students that when we say turn left or right, we're giving directions from the bird's point of view.\r\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "9348cae3-4fe2-46af-bf64-d7f8afcf9a26",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7684f284-70a6-4c67-8ca0-9220f05970f7"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "56574b18-a515-4bcf-b7bd-d9c676b4b026",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-list-alt\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Display**: Show “Preview Online Puzzle” slide\n\n**Model:** Pull up Puzzle 5 to do in front of the class. This will be the same puzzle that they just saw in the bridging activity. While working through this puzzle with the class, remind students that making mistakes is okay and remind them that the only way to be successful is to be persistent.  \n\n**Discuss:** _Does anyone remember how to solve this puzzle?_\n\nAs the teacher, you should decide if you will have the students remind you how to solve it from their seats, or come to the computer to drag the actual blocks in one-by-one.\n\n**Transition:** Now that students have seen an online puzzle in practice, they should be ready to start solving puzzles of their own.  Continue to the lab or bring out their classroom computers."
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "56574b18-a515-4bcf-b7bd-d9c676b4b026",
        "lesson_activity.key": "7684f284-70a6-4c67-8ca0-9220f05970f7"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "4977431e-fa92-4fb3-a73f-ddefa167a9fd",
      "position": 1,
      "properties": {
        "name": "Programming with Angry Birds",
        "tips": [
          {
            "type": "teachingTip",
            "markdown": "Show the students the right way to help classmates:\r\n\r\n - Don’t sit in the classmate’s chair\r\n - Don’t use the classmate’s keyboard\r\n - Don’t touch the classmate’s mouse\r\n - Make sure the classmate can describe the solution to you out loud before you walk away\r\n"
          }
        ]
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "4977431e-fa92-4fb3-a73f-ddefa167a9fd",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1ef67755-63da-445a-bbcd-8c0411c54719"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "0b46b08f-0553-447f-afb9-9bcf3006f8f1",
      "position": 2,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-list-alt\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Display**: Show “Maze Intro: Programming with Blocks” video",
        "progression_name": "Video: Maze Intro - Programming with Blocks "
      },
      "seeding_key": {
        "activity_section.key": "0b46b08f-0553-447f-afb9-9bcf3006f8f1",
        "lesson_activity.key": "1ef67755-63da-445a-bbcd-8c0411c54719"
      }
    },
    {
      "key": "18ed9bc9-ad15-4317-bee9-7c9416724a34",
      "position": 3,
      "properties": {
        "description": "<i class=\"fa fa-list-alt\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Display**: Show “Decompose it!” slide\n\nRemind students to break each puzzle down into smaller steps.\n\n<i class=\"fa fa-list-alt\" aria-hidden=\"true\"></i> **Display**: Show “Level 2-7 - Skill Building” slide",
        "progression_name": "Skill Building"
      },
      "seeding_key": {
